Q: How do I run a Node.js app as a background service? A: <p>You can run your node app in background with <code>&amp;</code> in unix. Make sure your node app should not have any interactive mode like receive data from input.</p>
<pre class="lang-bash prettyprint-override"><code>node src/index.js -p 1234 --another-options &amp;
</code></pre>

Q: Kendo ui grid with custom filter A: <p>You could use the <a href="http://docs.telerik.com/kendo-ui/api/web/grid#events-filterMenuInit" rel="nofollow">filterMenuInit</a> event of the Grid to attach a click handler to the "Clear"
and "filter" button.</p>

<p>for Clear button in </p>

<pre><code>function filterMenuInit(e) {
    e.container.on("click", "[type='reset']", function () {
        alert("Clear button clicked");
    });
}
</code></pre>
